                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "5/10\nA disappointing follow up to a decent classic survival horror. This time set in a college instead of a high school, which means the stereotypical school characters and themes are dialed up to 11. A lot of the story elements and character tropes are centered around drugs and sex, so be prepared for a lot of cringe. The story in the first game wasn't the greatest thing ever, but in this game its just bad. All of the new characters are awful, and the 3 returning characters are also worse, apart from Stan who's only virtue is dropping the ghetto talk he had in the first game.\nGameplay is similar to the first. You control 2 characters at a time from a larger pool, all with different abilities and the game can be played in co-op, which is about the only virtue because this game is more co-op friendly than the first game. Combat and how the camera works is somewhat modernized and is in an odd position of trying to be classic and modern survival horror at the same time, doing neither well. The other problem is the player has no choice in which characters are used, which means their abilities are just used as set pieces. The other problem is character deaths are all scripted, rather than based on player actions. And maybe that's a good thing since you'll likely be hoping that most of them bite the bullet with how annoying most of them are.\nI will say one thing, the atmosphere is better and makes better use of lighting and sound making the game a little creepy than the original. The game is also a little longer, though it is also far more linear.\nIn general, I wouldn't recommend this one unless you just really enjoyed the first game enough to see how the story ends, this game isn't worth it. \n",
